{%- set faqs = [
  ["What does a penetration testing services company in Bangalore do?", "A penetration testing services company in Bangalore simulates real attacks on your applications, APIs, and networks with your permission. The goal is to find exploitable weaknesses, explain their business impact, and give your team prioritized fixes, followed by verification that those fixes work."],
  ["How is penetration testing pricing determined?", "Penetration testing pricing depends on scope: the number of applications, APIs, and network assets, their complexity, and the depth of testing required. We define scope first, then provide a quotation that reflects your actual environment rather than a fixed package."],
  ["What is the difference between vulnerability scanning and penetration testing?", "Scanning uses automated tools to list potential weaknesses. Penetration testing adds manual work to confirm which weaknesses can actually be exploited and what an attacker could reach. You get fewer false positives and a clearer view of real risk."],
  ["What does website penetration testing cover compared with web application penetration testing services?", "Website penetration testing focuses on public-facing sites, including forms, upload functions, admin areas, and configuration. Web application penetration testing services go deeper into authentication, authorization, and business logic in interactive applications. Many clients need both, and we scope them together."],
  ["When do we need network penetration testing?", "Network penetration testing is valuable before audits, after infrastructure changes, and when you expose new services to the internet. It shows whether attackers can breach your perimeter or move laterally once inside your internal network."],
  ["How should we choose between penetration testing companies?", "Ask each provider how much of the work is manual, what the report contains, whether developers get a walkthrough, and whether retesting is included. We include manual testing, actionable reporting, developer walkthroughs, and one retest as standard."],
  ["Do you retest after we fix the vulnerabilities?", "Yes. Our published offering includes one retest. After your team implements fixes, we verify them and update the report, so you can show auditors and customers that identified issues are actually resolved."]
] %}
